{
  "schema": "anim.reactions/1",
  "_about": "Hit reactions with variety (docs/animation/hit-reactions.md). Until now every blow drew the same two flinch poses with a body region's additive pose; here each blow picks a variant by its weight, the way it came and the body part it hit, and never the one the last blow picked. A variant is a set of bone turns (radians about x, y, z, in the bone's own frame: z pitches, y turns, x rolls) scaled by the blow's weight and shaped by an envelope (in over `attack` seconds, held `hold`, out by `dur`), plus how much of the generic flinch it replaces (`base`, 0 to 1), the body's own push along the blow (`dx`, `dy`) and a hips drop. Pitch turns are in the away-from-the-blow frame: positive tips the part away (a front blow's head goes back), and a blow from behind mirrors them; yaw and roll take a side from the blow's own draw. `weight`: light (force under `light_max`), medium (to `medium_max`), heavy (over). `region`: head, core, arms, legs or any. `dir`: front, back or any. `vert`: up (the blow lifts him), level, down (the blow drives him down) or any. After the variant a recovery (`recover`, by weight) draws the body getting itself back: a nod, a shake of the head, a breath. Every envelope's attack is 0.05 s or more and every recovery ramp 6 ticks or more (the snappy profile solves on twos). Under reduced motion the turns are 0.6. Render only, outside the sim's data hash. First values, Animation's.",
  "light_max": 0.5,
  "medium_max": 1.0,
  "attack": 0.05,
